## Time above threshold

In this section we calculate the time above threshold for the single day of `22 September 2025`, depending on latitude and country. We require the `local_time` variable for that. Because we unnested the data into the participant data, that information is available to us.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
TAT250 <- 
light_data |> 
  filter_Date(start = "2025-09-22", #<1>
              length = "1 day", #<1>
              Datetime.colname = local_time) |> #<1>
  dplyr::summarize(
    duration_above_threshold( #<2>
      LIGHT, local_time, threshold = 250, na.rm = TRUE, #<2>
      as.df = TRUE #<2>
    ),
    latitude = first(latitude), #<3>
    longitude = first(longitude), #<3>
    country = first(country) #<3>
  ) |> 
  mutate(n = n(), .by = country) #<4>

TAT250 |> head()
```

